From: Ahnaf Shahriar <ahnaf.shahriar@neuralink.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NRF52840_GPIO: Fix external input lost when pin has pull-up

When a GPIO connector drives a pin to its default state (e.g., LOW)
before the firmware configures it, the InputValue setter early-returns
because the value matches the existing State[] (both are false after
reset).  This leaves everSet=true but State[] unchanged.

Later, when firmware configures the pin with NRF_GPIO_PIN_PULLUP,
DefaultValue is set to true.  Since everSet is true, GetCurrentValue()
returns State[] (false) — which appears correct.

However, if the connector never fires because the driving pin never
transitions (STM32 PA6 starts at 0, stays at 0), OnGPIO is never
called, everSet stays false, and GetCurrentValue() returns
DefaultValue (true = pull-up).  The external LOW is invisible.

The fix ensures the first external write always updates State[],
even if the value matches the current (uninitialized) state.  This
guarantees the external drive is recorded and overrides the pull-up
default on subsequent reads.

Also adds null-conditional to PinChanged event invocation for safety.

---
 .../GPIOPort/NRF52840_GPIO.cs                 | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/GPIOPort/NRF52840_GPIO.cs b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/GPIOPort/NRF52840_GPIO.cs
index b45c15f9b..ebe823c57 100644
--- a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/GPIOPort/NRF52840_GPIO.cs
+++ b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/GPIOPort/NRF52840_GPIO.cs
@@ -246,23 +246,23 @@ public bool InputValue
 
                 set
                 {
+                    var wasEverSet = everSet;
                     everSet = true;
 
                     if(Direction != PinDirection.Input)
                     {
-                        // buffer the value so that it can be used on a next direction change
                         bufferedInputValue = value;
                         return;
                     }
 
-                    if(value == Parent.State[Id])
+                    if(wasEverSet && value == Parent.State[Id])
                     {
                         return;
                     }
 
                     Parent.NoisyLog("Setting pin {0} input to {1}", Id, value);
                     Parent.State[Id] = value;
-                    Parent.PinChanged(this, value);
+                    Parent.PinChanged?.Invoke(this, value);
                     Parent.UpdateDetect();
                 }
             }
